{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c3ef9629-f5d3-466d-b5c1-4be4674901e6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b7a2cd3897e2522","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-s8yw2uip/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E006.md","content":"# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n\n## Description\n\nA gating CI check that fails any serving-stack build which reintroduces non-validated crypto usage, so the FIPS-remediated state of the model serving stack cannot regress unnoticed. The check is developed independently of the remediation work and runs gating in the serving-stack build pipelines, including the Platform Operator pipeline once that component is onboarded.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the regression check: detection of non-validated crypto usage in the images produced by serving-stack builds.\n- Wire the check as a gating step in the serving-stack build pipelines (Konflux), covering KServe builds and the Platform Operator builds.\n- Define the check's failure output so an offending build identifies the non-validated usage it introduced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage fails the gating check, with output identifying the offending usage.\n- The check runs as a gating step in the serving-stack build pipelines, covering both KServe and Platform Operator builds.\n- The check passes on the FIPS-remediated serving-stack images (no false positives on the remediated state).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (primary): \"CI enforces FIPS regressions: a gating check fails any serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\"\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70496,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-871b8a555f0b9529","agent