ed by engineering effort; they dominate the delivery schedule for certified compliance (strategy problem statement and open-questions note). The engineering deliverable this epic controls is the assembled, submitted package — the certification outcome arrives on the laboratory's schedule.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (primary): \"A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\"\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70971,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-871b8a555f0b9529","agent_id":"a7de8b91c40c6b063","session_id":"29cb84a9-828d-4dcd-a97c-1ceca07010da","uuid":"e7d73f7d-e88b-412c-8dbd-25a8318887d5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:52:24.664Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013"}
