ack images and the remediation applied to each.\n45\t- All KServe serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters, with no non-validated crypto in the request path, verified by tests executed on a FIPS-enabled cluster.\n46\t- Serving behavior on non-FIPS clusters is unchanged (regression verification).\n47\t- The existing Konflux build pipeline builds the remediated KServe images green.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 (primary): KServe share of \"all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters using validated crypto modules (no non-validated crypto in the request path)\".\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a67fb82ef65b8ab9","agent_id":"ae8e7d484f6c05143","session_id":"29cb84a9-828d-4dcd-a97c-1ceca07010da","uuid":"27e6ab44-657d-4c2a-b398-e31c9d0a0b59","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:54:46.909Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ac030a12ea133cc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
