{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-975c71b695de2448","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E006\n3\ttitle: CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# CI gating check for FIPS crypto regressions in serving-stack builds\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tA gating CI check that fails any serving-stack build which reintroduces non-validated crypto usage, so the FIPS-remediated state of the model serving stack cannot regress unnoticed. The check is developed independently of the remediation work and runs gating in the serving-stack build pipelines, including the Platform Operator pipeline once that component is onboarded.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Implement the regression check: detection of non-validated crypto usage in the images produced by serving-stack builds.\n38\t- Wire the check as a gating step in the serving-stack build pipelines (Konflux), covering KServe builds and the Platform Operator builds.\n39\t- Define the check's failure output so an offending build identifies the non-validated usage it introduced.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage fails the gating check, with output identifying the offending usage.\n44\t- The check runs as a gating step in the serving-stack build pipelines, covering both KServe and Platform Operator builds.\n45\t- The check passes on the FIPS-remediated serving-stack images (no false positives on the remediated state).\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-3 (primary): \"CI enforces FIPS regressions: a gating check fails any serving-stack build that reintroduces non-validated crypto usage.\"\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a67fb82ef65b8ab9","agent_id":"ae8e7d484f6c05143","session_id":"29cb84a9-828d-4dcd-a97c-1ceca07010da","uuid":"5e062b69-92f5-483b-9fa9-186e96dec8ea","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:54:50.521Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-975c71b695de2448","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
