{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85e1950b2d5cd049","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E007\n3\ttitle: FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E004\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E005\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 0\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: -1\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\timplementation_type: null\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 2\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package and submission\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tAssemble the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving stack — the crypto module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and submit it through the security review board to the external accredited certification laboratory. The package is assembled once the serving-stack remediation work has produced its outcomes; the build attestations are consumed as content from the serving-stack Konflux build pipelines.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Compile the module inventory of cryptographic modules across the serving-stack images from the remediation outcomes (KServe and Platform Operator).\n40\t- Collect the signed build attestations produced by the serving-stack Konflux build pipelines, including the Platform Operator pipeline.\n41\t- Collect the FIPS-enabled-cluster test results produced by the remediation work.\n42\t- Assemble the package in the form the security review board and certification laboratory require, and submit it through the review board to the lab.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- The evidence package contains the complete module inventory, the signed build attestations from the serving-stack build pipelines, and the FIPS-enabled-cluster test results for the remediated images.\n47\t- The evidence package is submitted through the security review board to the external certification laboratory and triaged at intake.\n48\t\n49\t## Risks / Notes\n50\t\n51\t- Certification-laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months, and security-review-board sign-off occurs at defined milestones. Both are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort; they dominate the delivery schedule for certified compliance (strategy problem statement and open-questions note). The engineering deliverable this epic controls is the assembled, submitted package — the certification outcome arrives on the laboratory's schedule.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-2 (primary): \"A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\"\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a67fb82ef65b8ab9","agent_id":"ae8e7d484f6c05143","session_id":"29cb84a9-828d-4dcd-a97c-1ceca07010da","uuid":"be4a72fa-250d-453d-a472-8f665514529a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:54:53.912Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85e1950b2d5cd049","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
