{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8528b362b569030e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9013\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: Acceptance Criteria Quality\n9\t  description: E007 second AC includes \"and triaged at intake\" — intake triage is\n10\t    performed by the external certification laboratory on its own schedule, an externally\n11\t    controlled outcome misfiled as an AC. Trim the AC to the epic own deliverable\n12\t    (package assembled and submitted through the security review board) and move the\n13\t    intake/certification expectation to Risks/Notes.\n14\terror: null\n15\t---\n16\t## Review Summary\n17\t\n18\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n19\tRecommendation: accept\n20\t\n21\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py` exited 0 — body sections,\n22\tcanonical components, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance, and\n23\tRules 7/8/10 parallelism all pass). Triage check: `triage: null` (full\n24\tdecomposition), so the 8-epic output is expected. No conditional branch files.\n25\tGraded below is only what the validator cannot check.\n26\t\n27\t## Criterion Details\n28\t\n29\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n30\tAll four HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 (P0) → E004 + E005 (component split) with\n31\tE001–E003 as enabling epics; HLR-2 (P0) → E007; HLR-3 (P1) → E006; HLR-4 (P2) →\n32\tE008, covered rather than deferred. Every epic carries an HLR Traceability\n33\tsection and the summary matrix is complete with no orphaned requirements.\n34\tPriority inheritance is sound: the only P1 epic (E006) blocks solely the\n35\tdocs-authoring epic E008, which is exempt from priority inheritance. E008's P0\n36\tpriority via the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Critical) is\n37\tcorrectly applied and explained in both the epic-list notes and Health Warnings.\n38\tNo priority collapse: each HLR maps to its own epic(s) at a single priority\n39\tlevel, so no bundling analysis was required.\n40\t\n41\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n42\tFrontmatter `dependencies` match the summary DAG diagram edge-for-edge in both\n43\tdirections (E001→E003, E001→E005, E002→E005, E004→E007, E005→E007, and\n44\tE001–E007→E008). Arrows follow the dependency→dependent convention. No cycles,\n45\tno references to nonexistent epics, no branch-file dependencies.\n46\tImplementation-type parallelism is fully respected: E002∥E001 (Rule 7),\n47\tE002∥E003 (Rule 8), and E003∥E005 (Rule 10) have no edges in either direction;\n48\tthe E005 coupling is the Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC, exactly as\n49\tmandated. E003∥E007 and E003∥E006 are also correctly edge-free — the pipeline's\n50\tattestations and gating are consumed as content/AC gates on E007 and E006, the\n51\trule-compliant shape (not a missing artifact edge). The E001→E005 and E002→E005\n52\tedges are justified (repo and license verdict genuinely precondition the\n53\tPlatform Operator's remediation code) and do not serialize KServe work (E004 is\n54\tindependent). Critical path E001→E005→E007→E008 (length 4) fits the\n55\tmedium-with-new-component heuristic (4–5).\n56\t\n57\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n58\tComponent/team tuples are clean: E001–E003, E005 (Platform Operator / RHOAI\n59\tPlatform), E004, E006, E007 (KServe / RHOAI Serving), E008 (Documentation /\n60\tRHOAI Docs). E006 and E007 each touch both strategy components, but each is one\n61\tlogical change (one CI check; one evidence package with one submission path) —\n62\tsplitting either by component would create two epics building the same surface,\n63\tand the spans are explicitly recorded in Component Mapping Notes rather than\n64\tsilently dropped. No scope duplication between E004 and E005 (disjoint image\n65\tsets); E007 consumes the inventories rather than rebuilding them. No work-product\n66\ttype mixing — docs authoring is isolated in E008. E004's size overage (\"several\n67\timages\", volume unknown until inventory) is a managed watch item, not a defect:\n68\tHealth Warnings #5 records a concrete re-split trigger (re-split by image group\n69\tif the completed inventory exceeds one sprint), which is the required shape.\n70\t\n71\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n72\tAll eight epics are Implementation and each produces a concrete artifact\n73\t(repository, license verdict, pipeline onboarding, remediated images, CI check,\n74\tsubmitted package, published docs). No `gated_by` is set anywhere and no epic\n75\tdepends on an Investigation, so gating metadata is trivially consistent. The\n76\tInvestigation Analysis correctly argues the two candidate unknowns are not\n77\tstructural: the crypto module inventory determines remediation volume inside\n78\tE004/E005 (captured as ACs), and lab/review-board timing is a schedule\n79\tconstraint recorded on E007's Risks/Notes — neither changes which epics exist.\n80\tThe Platform Operator repo-existence discrepancy is absorbed into E001's\n81\treduce-to-validation AC rather than a speculative Investigation.\n82\t\n83\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n84\tAll eight epics are Implementation type and carry `ai_signals` (no\n85\t`investigation_signals` misapplication); all eight `-ai-signals.md` rationale\n86\tfiles exist and their values match frontmatter. Spot-checks against the rubric\n87\tand `.context`: E004/E006/E007/E008 score `architecture_claims: 1` citing\n88\t`architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md` (which does corroborate Konflux onboarding,\n89\tmidstream repos, and the serving role), while E001/E002/E003/E005 score 0 with\n90\tthe correct rationale — no context file covers Platform Operator, so the\n91\tstrategy's premise can be neither corroborated nor contradicted. E007's\n92\t`external_dependency: -1` / `human_process_gates: -1` (lab, review board) and\n93\tE008's `human_process_gates: -1` (technical review sign-off) are well grounded\n94\tin the strategy. `open_questions: 1` across epics is consistent with the\n95\tstrategy's \"None on scope\" declaration. No computed-score arithmetic was\n96\tchecked, per the pipeline-computes rule.\n97\t\n98\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n99\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs are\n100\tpresent: E005 carries the Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC for the\n101\tkonflux-onboarding coupling; E003 produces signed attestations retrievable for\n102\tthe evidence package; E008 carries the technical-review sign-off AC; E007's AC\n103\tincludes the attestations as content (the AC-gate shape Rules 13/25 require).\n104\tE004/E005 verify on FIPS-enabled clusters with non-FIPS regression checks.\n105\tExternal lab turnaround and review-board cadence are correctly kept in\n106\tRisks/Notes and Health Warnings, not as ACs. No draft-ID references in epic\n107\tbodies. One minor finding: E007's second AC ends with \"and triaged at intake\" —\n108\tintake triage is performed by the external laboratory on its own schedule, so\n109\tthat clause is an externally controlled outcome misfiled as an AC; the AC should\n110\tstop at the epic's own deliverable (assembly and submission through the review\n111\tboard), with the intake/certification expectation in Risks/Notes.\n112\t\n113\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n114\tThe full strategy scope is accounted for: FIPS remediation of both affected\n115\tcomponents (E004, E005), the evidence package with submission path (E007), CI\n116\tregression enforcement (E006, covering both KServe and Platform Operator\n117\tbuilds), and documentation of posture and cluster prerequisites (E008).\n118\tOut-of-scope items (workbenches, pipelines, training, Common Criteria) are\n119\tcorrectly absent. Strategy-level context is carried forward: the external\n120\tschedule gates appear in E007's Risks/Notes and Health Warnings; the\n121\tPlatform Operator inventory discrepancy is flagged with human-verification\n122\tguidance and a both-cases plan in E001; missing strategy sections (teams,\n123\tdependencies, NFRs) are disclosed in Health Warnings #1. The Tiered Delivery\n124\tsection correctly separates independently shippable value (Tier 1) from the\n125\texternally gated certification outcome (Tier 2). No conditional branches were\n126\trequired and none are missing.\n127\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac2dc8c8f1dff594","agent_id":"af9e2b0c7e49be959","session_id":"29cb84a9-828d-4dcd-a97c-1ceca07010da","uuid":"ce9fa889-c6f1-408d-b439-c92c181b40b8","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:57:50.847Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8528b362b569030e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
