downstream build and remediation work can proceed.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- A midstream Platform Operator repository exists under opendatahub-io (or a pre-existing one is identified and validated), mirroring the upstream source at a recorded state.\n44\t- The repository follows the standard opendatahub-io midstream conventions applied to peer components.\n45\t- The repository state (new vs. pre-existing) and the pinned upstream source are recorded for the downstream build-pipeline onboarding.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- HLR-1 (enabling): provides the midstream repository foundation required to remediate the Platform Operator's serving-stack images for FIPS-enabled clusters.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a488ada2fd1a9b9e","agent_id":"af6c989a891c2acf9","session_id":"29cb84a9-828d-4dcd-a97c-1ceca07010da","uuid":"54eb1a84-f3fd-4fdb-a92c-bea75582da25","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:59:09.953Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b5f2b39e8c25237","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
