{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be93e7bd25601d0","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E002.md:33:Validate the licenses of the Platform Operator component's transitive dependency tree ahead of its FIPS remediation. License problems discovered after implementation starts would force dependency changes that alter the remediation approach, so the scan runs up front, in parallel with repository onboarding.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E002.md:45:- The license verdict is available to the Platform Operator FIPS remediation work before it builds against the dependency set.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md:3:title: Platform Operator midstream repository onboarding\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md:9:implementation_type: repo-onboarding\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md:29:# Platform Operator midstream repository onboarding\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md:33:Establish the midstream repository for the Platform Operator component under the opendatahub-io organization. The Platform Operator is listed as an affected component of the FIPS 140-3 compliance strategy, but the platform's architecture-context inventory has no file for it, so it is treated as a component not yet in the platform and provisioned through the standard onboarding chain. This epic provides the repository foundation that the Platform Operator's build-pipeline onboarding and FIPS remediation work build on.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md:45:- The repository state (new vs. pre-existing) and the pinned upstream source are recorded for the downstream build-pipeline onboarding.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md:3:title: Platform Operator Konflux build pipeline onboarding\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md:9:implementation_type: konflux-onboarding\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md:30:# Platform Operator Konflux build pipeline onboarding\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md:34:Onboard the Platform Operator's midstream repository to the Konflux build pipeline so the component's images are built through the platform's standard pipeline, with the provenance and attestation capabilities the compliance evidence package consumes. This work starts once the midstream repository exists.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md:38:- Konflux onboarding configuration for the Platform Operator repository (application and component definitions, build recipe), following the standard onboarding recipe.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md:44:- The Platform Operator repository is onboarded to Konflux following the standard onboarding recipe.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E005.md:35:Remove non-validated cryptographic library usage from the Platform Operator's images so the operator runs correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters using validated crypto modules. This work starts once the component's midstream repository exists and its dependency licenses have been validated; it proceeds in parallel with the component's build-pipeline onboarding, with the pipeline coupling enforced by a \"build pipeline green\" acceptance criterion rather than a scheduling dependency.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E006.md:33:A gating CI check that fails any serving-stack build which reintroduces non-validated crypto usage, so the FIPS-remediated state of the model serving stack cannot regress unnoticed. The check is developed independently of the remediation work and runs gating in the serving-stack build pipelines, including the Platform Operator pipeline once that component is onboarded.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E007.md:35:Assemble the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the model serving stack — the crypto module inventory, build attestations, and test results — and submit it through the security review board to the external accredited certification laboratory. The package is assembled once the serving-stack remediation work has produced its outcomes; the build attestations are consumed as content from the serving-stack Konflux build pipelines.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E007.md:42:- Assemble the package in the form the security review board and certification laboratory require, and submit it through the review board to the lab.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E007.md:47:- The evidence package is submitted through the security review board to the external certification laboratory.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E007.md:51:- Certification-laboratory turnaround is historically six to nine months, and security-review-board sign-off occurs at defined milestones. Both are externally controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort; they dominate the delivery schedule for certified compliance (strategy problem statement and open-questions note). The engineering deliverable this epic controls is the assembled, submitted package — the certification outcome arrives on the laboratory's schedule.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E007.md:52:- Once submitted, the certification laboratory triages the package at intake on its own schedule. Intake triage and the certification verdict are externally controlled outcomes, not deliverables of this epic; this epic's deliverable ends at a complete package submitted through the security review board.\nartifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E007.md:56:- HLR-2 (primary): \"A compliance evidence package (module inventory, build attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the security review board to the external certification lab.\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a488ada2fd1a9b9e","agent_id":"af6c989a891c2acf9","session_id":"29cb84a9-828d-4dcd-a97c-1ceca07010da","uuid":"49ff564a-5ba6-432e-9ee9-6dbbfa3746c5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:00:59.319Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be93e7bd25601d0","permission_decision":{"decision":"acce